# bitch configuration — deploy/setup.sh writes /etc/bitch/bitch.env from this
# (prompting for the required values). By hand: copy there, fill in, chmod 600.
# This file holds secrets (§4.2). NEVER commit the real one; .env* is gitignored.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Telegram bot token from @BotFather. Treat like a root credential (§4.2).
BITCH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN=123456:ABC-your-bot-token

# Hard allowlist of numeric Telegram user IDs (§4.1). Comma-separated.
# Find yours by messaging @userinfobot. NOT usernames — numeric IDs.
BITCH_ALLOWED_USERS=111111111

# Workspace jail roots (§4.3). Colon/comma-separated absolute paths. Edits and
# file reads are confined here; path traversal outside is denied at every tier.
BITCH_ROOTS=/srv/work

# --- Anthropic auth (exactly one; used by the claude CLI) ------------------
# An API key (pay per token), or a subscription token from running
# `claude setup-token` on your own machine. setup.sh fills in whichever you give.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=sk-ant-oat...

# --- Optional (defaults shown) ----------------------------------------------

# Initial working directory for a new session (must be within BITCH_ROOTS).
# Defaults to the first root.
# BITCH_DEFAULT_DIR=/srv/work

# Default model and effort (§9.1). These are the per-session defaults; each chat
# can override them live with /model and /effort. Develop plumbing on a cheaper
# model, run real work on Opus.
# BITCH_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# BITCH_EFFORT=high            # low|medium|high|xhigh|max

# Absolute path to the claude CLI if it isn't on the service PATH.
# BITCH_CLAUDE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/claude

# Extra flags passed through to `claude` verbatim (advanced).
# BITCH_CLAUDE_EXTRA_ARGS=

# Starting permission tier 0..3 (§4.3). Start constrained.
# BITCH_DEFAULT_TIER=1

# How long an approval waits before defaulting to deny, seconds (§4.3).
# BITCH_APPROVAL_TIMEOUT=300

# Per-day USD budget; 0 disables the guard (§4.4).
# BITCH_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=20

# --- Voice input (§7) -------------------------------------------------------
# Unset ⇒ voice notes are declined. Set the URL and a voice note becomes a turn:
# the bridge uploads the audio to an OpenAI-compatible
# POST /v1/audio/transcriptions and runs the transcript as the prompt.
#
# PRIVACY: this is the one thing that sends your data to a third party you
# choose — the recording leaves the box. Point it at whoever you're willing to
# hear you, including a self-hosted endpoint on 127.0.0.1. The key is
# bridge-only: it is never passed to the agent's process (§4.6).
#
# Must be https, unless the endpoint is on this machine. Groq, OpenAI, speaches
# and LocalAI all serve this shape.
# BITCH_TRANSCRIBE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/audio/transcriptions
# BITCH_TRANSCRIBE_KEY=sk-...   # optional — omit for a keyless local endpoint
# BITCH_TRANSCRIBE_MODEL=whisper-1

# Loopback address for the permission-hook callback server (§4.3). Bind to
# localhost only — no inbound app ports (§3).
# BITCH_HOOK_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8765

# Shared secret gating the loopback server. Auto-generated per boot if empty;
# set it explicitly only if you want it stable across restarts.
# BITCH_HOOK_SECRET=

# SQLite session store and scratch state dir (§6). Relative to WorkingDirectory.
# Inbound attachments land in <BITCH_STATE_DIR>/media (§7) and that dir is added
# to the jail roots so the agent can read them; it has no env var of its own —
# a movable media root would be one more path to reason about against the roots.
# BITCH_DB_PATH=data/bitch.sqlite
# BITCH_STATE_DIR=data/state
